{
  "id": "a1b2c3d4-htb1-recon-0001-000000000001",
  "name": "htb-recon",
  "description": "HTB reconnaissance workflow - scans target and enumerates discovered services",
  "flowchart": {
    "blocks": {
      "start-001": {
        "id": "start-001",
        "type": "start",
        "name": "START",
        "position": {
          "x": 200,
          "y": 50
        }
      },
      "recon-001": {
        "id": "recon-001",
        "type": "prompt",
        "name": "RUSTSCAN RECON",
        "position": {
          "x": 200,
          "y": 150
        },
        "prompt": "Run a comprehensive rustscan on target $1.\n\nRun: rustscan -a $1 -- -sV -sC\n\nRustscan will quickly scan all 65535 ports and pass open ports to nmap for service detection. This is much faster than pure nmap.\n\nIf rustscan is not available, fall back to: nmap -sV -sC -p- $1\n\nAfter the scan completes, analyze the results and identify:\n1. All open ports and services\n2. Service versions where detected\n3. Any interesting findings from NSE scripts\n4. Potential attack vectors based on services found\n\nWhat services were discovered?",
        "output_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "services": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "port": {
                    "type": "integer"
                  },
                  "service": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "version": {
                    "type": "string"
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            "hasWeb": {
              "type": "boolean"
            },
            "hasSMB": {
              "type": "boolean"
            },
            "hasSSH": {
              "type": "boolean"
            },
            "hasFTP": {
              "type": "boolean"
            },
            "potentialVectors": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "services",
            "hasWeb",
            "hasSMB",
            "hasSSH",
            "hasFTP",
            "potentialVectors"
          ]
        },
        "sound_effect": null
      },
      "branch-web-001": {
        "id": "branch-web-001",
        "type": "branch",
        "name": "HAS WEB?",
        "position": {
          "x": 200,
          "y": 300
        },
        "condition": "hasWeb"
      },
      "enum-web-001": {
        "id": "enum-web-001",
        "type": "prompt",
        "name": "WEB ENUM",
        "position": {
          "x": 400,
          "y": 300
        },
        "prompt": "Web service detected on $1. Perform web enumeration:\n\n1. Check what's on the main page (curl or browser)\n2. Look for robots.txt, sitemap.xml\n3. Run directory enumeration: gobuster dir -u http://$1 -w /usr/share/wordlists/dirb/common.txt (or feroxbuster)\n4. Check for common files: .git, .env, backup files, etc.\n5. Identify the technology stack (headers, whatweb, wappalyzer)\n6. Look for subdomains if there's a hostname\n\nIf HTTPS is available, check that too.\n\nReport your findings.",
        "output_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "webFindings": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "directories": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "technologies": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "interestingFiles": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "webFindings",
            "directories",
            "technologies"
          ]
        },
        "sound_effect": null
      },
      "branch-smb-001": {
        "id": "branch-smb-001",
        "type": "branch",
        "name": "HAS SMB?",
        "position": {
          "x": 200,
          "y": 450
        },
        "condition": "hasSMB"
      },
      "enum-smb-001": {
        "id": "enum-smb-001",
        "type": "prompt",
        "name": "SMB ENUM",
        "position": {
          "x": 400,
          "y": 450
        },
        "prompt": "SMB service detected on $1. Perform SMB enumeration:\n\n1. List shares: smbclient -L //$1 -N\n2. Try anonymous access to shares\n3. Run enum4linux: enum4linux -a $1\n4. Check for known vulnerabilities (EternalBlue, etc.)\n5. Look for accessible files, credentials, or sensitive info\n\nReport your findings.",
        "output_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "smbFindings": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "shares": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "accessibleFiles": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "credentials": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "smbFindings",
            "shares"
          ]
        },
        "sound_effect": null
      },
      "branch-ftp-001": {
        "id": "branch-ftp-001",
        "type": "branch",
        "name": "HAS FTP?",
        "position": {
          "x": 200,
          "y": 600
        },
        "condition": "hasFTP"
      },
      "enum-ftp-001": {
        "id": "enum-ftp-001",
        "type": "prompt",
        "name": "FTP ENUM",
        "position": {
          "x": 400,
          "y": 600
        },
        "prompt": "FTP service detected on $1. Perform FTP enumeration:\n\n1. Try anonymous login: ftp $1 (user: anonymous)\n2. List accessible files and directories\n3. Check for writable directories\n4. Download any interesting files\n5. Check FTP version for known vulnerabilities\n\nReport your findings.",
        "output_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "ftpFindings": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "anonymousAccess": {
              "type": "boolean"
            },
            "files": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "writable": {
              "type": "boolean"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "ftpFindings",
            "anonymousAccess"
          ]
        },
        "sound_effect": null
      },
      "report-001": {
        "id": "report-001",
        "type": "prompt",
        "name": "SAVE SERVICES",
        "position": {
          "x": 200,
          "y": 750
        },
        "prompt": "Recon complete for $1.\n\nSummarize all findings:\n- Services discovered: {{services}}\n- Web findings (if any): {{webFindings}}\n- SMB findings (if any): {{smbFindings}}\n- FTP findings (if any): {{ftpFindings}}\n\nTasks:\n1. Write a structured services.json to the current directory:\n\n{\n  \"target\": \"$1\",\n  \"scan_timestamp\": \"<current ISO timestamp>\",\n  \"services\": [\n    {\n      \"port\": <port number>,\n      \"protocol\": \"tcp|udp\",\n      \"service\": \"<service name>\",\n      \"version\": \"<version string if detected>\",\n      \"product\": \"<product name if detected>\",\n      \"extraInfo\": \"<any additional info from nmap scripts>\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"webServices\": [\n    {\n      \"port\": <port>,\n      \"url\": \"<base url>\",\n      \"title\": \"<page title>\",\n      \"technologies\": [\"<detected tech stack>\"],\n      \"directories\": [\"<discovered paths>\"],\n      \"interestingFiles\": [\"<notable files found>\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"findings\": {\n    \"web\": \"{{webFindings}}\",\n    \"smb\": \"{{smbFindings}}\",\n    \"ftp\": \"{{ftpFindings}}\"\n  }\n}\n\n2. Write human-readable summary to ./recon-report-$1.md\n\nProvide summary.",
        "output_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "summary": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "serviceCount": {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "servicesFileWritten": {
              "type": "boolean"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "summary",
            "serviceCount",
            "servicesFileWritten"
          ]
        },
        "sound_effect": null
      },
      "end-001": {
        "id": "end-001",
        "type": "end",
        "name": "END",
        "position": {
          "x": 200,
          "y": 900
        }
      }
    },
